\echo 'session463e (ascension-isaiah) — sweep starting...'
BEGIN;
CREATE TEMP TABLE _s463ei (xid INT, side CHAR(1), ob TEXT, oc INT, ov INT, nb TEXT, nc INT, nv INT, new_note TEXT, live_text TEXT, quotes_live BOOLEAN) ON COMMIT DROP;
INSERT INTO _s463ei VALUES
(4278,'T','ascension-isaiah',9,12,'ascension-isaiah',9,12,$n$*till the Beloved will descend in the form in which you will see Him descend will descend, I say into the world in the last days Yahuah (Lord), who will be called Messiah (Christ).* (Ascension of Isaiah 9:12). The pre-incarnation announcement of the Beloved's descent in human form — the prophetic-Christology that lands at Matt 1:23's *Immanuel — Elohim (God) with us.*$n$,$n$And he said unto me: "Crowns and thrones of glory they do not receive, till the Beloved will descend in the form in which you will see Him descend will descend, I say into the world in the last days Yahuah (Lord), who will be called Messiah (Christ).$n$,false),
(4315,'T','ascension-isaiah',4,2,'ascension-isaiah',4,2,$n$*Again, the devil taketh him up into an exceeding high mountain, and sheweth him all the kingdoms of the world, and the glory of them;* (Matthew 4:8). *After it is consummated, Beliar the great ruler, the king of this world, will descend, who hath ruled it since it came into being; yea, he will descent from his firmament in the likeness of a man, a lawless king, the slayer of his mother: who himself (even) this king.* (Ascension of Isaiah 4:2). The Ascension of Isaiah says that Beliar is the king of this world and has ruled it since it came into being. When the devil takes Yahusha (Jesus) up the mountain and shows him all the kingdoms of the world and their glory, he is showing what he holds for the present age, so the offer that follows was no empty boast. But the same passage speaks of the completion of the world, and a rule that was given for a season is a rule with an end.$n$,$n$After it is consummated, Beliar the great ruler, the king of this world, will descend, who hath ruled it since it came into being; yea, he will descent from his firmament in the likeness of a man, a lawless king, the slayer of his mother: who himself (even) this king.$n$,true),
(4316,'T','ascension-isaiah',4,9,'ascension-isaiah',4,9,$n$*And saith unto him, All these things will I give thee, if thou wilt fall down and worship me.* (Matthew 4:9). *And they will sacrifice to him and they will serve him saying: "This is Elohim (God) and beside him there is no other." And they greater number of those who shall have been associated together in order to receive the Beloved, he will turn aside after him.* (Ascension of Isaiah 4:8–9). Satan asks Yahusha (Jesus) for worship, and Yahusha (Jesus) refuses. The Ascension of Isaiah shows what the same ruler gets from the world in the days of the end: sacrifice and service, and the cry that there is no other god beside him, and then the greater number of those gathered to receive the Beloved turned aside after him. It is the same grab for worship, once refused by the Son in the wilderness, and then carried out on the many who do not hold fast.$n$,$n$And they greater number of those who shall have been associated together in order to receive the Beloved, he will turn aside after him.$n$,true),
(4317,'T','ascension-isaiah',1,3,'ascension-isaiah',3,13,$n$*Then saith Yahusha (Jesus) unto him, Get thee hence, Satan: for it is written, Thou shalt worship Yahuah Elohayka (the Lord thy God), and him only shalt thou serve.* (Matthew 4:10). *For Beliar was in great wrath against Isaiah by reason of the vision, and because of the exposure wherewith he had exposed Sammael, and because through him the going forth of the Beloved from the seventh heaven had been made known, and His transformation and His descent and the likeness into which He should be transformed (that is) the likeness of man, and the persecution wherewith he should be persecuted, and the torturers wherewith the children of Yashar'el (Israel) should torture Him, and the coming of His twelve disciples, and the teaching, and that He should before the sabbath be crucified upon the tree, and should be crucified together with wicked men, and that He should be buried in the sepulchre,* (Ascension of Isaiah 3:13). Beliar's rage against Isaiah is over one thing: the prophet had made known the Beloved's going forth from the seventh heaven and his descent in the likeness of man. In the wilderness the same adversary meets the Beloved now come down in that likeness, and is sent away with the commandment of Torah: worship Yahuah (the Lord) and serve him only. The one Beliar tried to keep hidden dismisses him with the Word.$n$,$n$For Beliar was in great wrath against Isaiah by reason of the vision, and because of the exposure wherewith he had exposed Sammael, and because through him the going forth of the Beloved from the seventh heaven had been made known, and His transformation and His descent and the likeness into which He should be transformed (that is) the likeness of man, and the persecution wherewith he should be persecuted, and the torturers wherewith the children of Yashar'el (Israel) should torture Him, and the coming of His twelve disciples, and the teaching, and that He should before the sabbath be crucified upon the tree, and should be crucified together with wicked men, and that He should be buried in the sepulchre,$n$,true),
(4457,'T','ascension-isaiah',4,3,'ascension-isaiah',4,3,$n$*Simon the Canaanite, and Judas Iscariot, who also betrayed him.* (Matthew 10:4). *Will persecute the plant which the Twelve Apostles of the Beloved have planted. Of the Twelve one will be delivered into his hands.* (Ascension of Isaiah 4:3). Before the Twelve are ever named, the Ascension of Isaiah says that the ruler of this world will persecute what they plant and that one of the Twelve will fall into his hands. Matthew's list of the apostles closes on exactly that note, with the last name carrying the word betrayed. Nothing in the account takes the Beloved by surprise. The persecution of the plant and the loss of one from the inner circle were spoken of ahead of time, and Matthew's commissioning of the Twelve goes on to warn them of what is coming.$n$,$n$Will persecute the plant which the Twelve Apostles of the Beloved have planted. Of the Twelve one will be delivered into his hands.$n$,true),
(4885,'T','ascension-isaiah',9,14,'ascension-isaiah',9,14,$n$*And they crucified him, and parted his garments, casting lots: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, They parted my garments among them, and upon my vesture did they cast lots.* (Matthew 27:35). *And the god of that world will stretch forth his hand against the Son, and they will crucify Him on a tree, and will slay Him not knowing who He is.* (Ascension of Isaiah 9:14). The Ascension of Isaiah puts the weight where it belongs. The one who stretches out his hand against the Son is the god of that world, the adversary behind the deed, and those who carry it out do so not knowing who He is. Matthew then tells it as it happened, that they crucified him and divided his garments, in keeping with what the prophet had said. The tree is the place of the curse that falls on a people for breaking the covenant, and the Son took that curse on himself, so that the scattered might come home to the Torah, not away from it.$n$,$n$And the god of that world will stretch forth his hand against the Son, and they will crucify Him on a tree, and will slay Him not knowing who He is.$n$,true),
(4886,'T','ascension-isaiah',9,16,'ascension-isaiah',9,16,$n$*Yahusha (Jesus), when he had cried again with a loud voice, yielded up the ghost.* (Matthew 27:50). *And when He hath plundered the angel of death, He will ascend on the third day, and he will remain in that world five hundred and forty-five days.* (Ascension of Isaiah 9:16). Matthew tells that Yahusha (Jesus) cried out and yielded up the ghost, and the verb is his own: he gave himself up. The Ascension of Isaiah says what that death was for. He goes down and plunders the angel of death, and on the third day he ascends. The death at the cross is the doorway of the descent, and the descent ends in the rising.$n$,$n$And when He hath plundered the angel of death, He will ascend on the third day, and he will remain in that world five hundred and forty-five days.$n$,true),
(4887,'T','ascension-isaiah',9,17,'ascension-isaiah',9,17,$n$*And the graves were opened; and many bodies of the saints which slept arose,* (Matthew 27:52). *And then many of the righteous will ascend with Him, whose spirits do not receive their garments till Yahuah (Lord) Messiah (Christ) ascend and they ascend with Him.* (Ascension of Isaiah 9:17). Matthew says the graves were opened and many bodies of the saints which slept arose. The Ascension of Isaiah says why the righteous waited as they did: their spirits do not receive their garments until the Messiah ascends, and then many of them ascend with him. Those who walked the covenant faithfully and slept are the first to be brought out when the way is opened, and the opened graves at the cross are a foretaste of the larger rising still to come.$n$,$n$And then many of the righteous will ascend with Him, whose spirits do not receive their garments till Yahuah (Lord) Messiah (Christ) ascend and they ascend with Him.$n$,true),
(4888,'T','ascension-isaiah',11,20,'ascension-isaiah',11,20,$n$*And they crucified him, and parted his garments, casting lots: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, They parted my garments among them, and upon my vesture did they cast lots.* (Matthew 27:35). *In Jerusalem indeed I saw Him being crucified on a tree:* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:20). Matthew tells of the crucifixion in a few plain lines and says it came to pass according to what was spoken by the prophet. The Ascension of Isaiah has Isaiah himself seeing it first, and naming the place: in Jerusalem, on a tree. What Matthew sets down as history, the prophet was shown beforehand.$n$,$n$In Jerusalem indeed I saw Him being crucified on a tree:$n$,true),
(4889,'T','ascension-isaiah',11,19,'ascension-isaiah',11,19,$n$*And laid it in his own new tomb, which he had hewn out in the rock: and he rolled a great stone to the door of the sepulchre, and departed.* (Matthew 27:60). *And after this the adversary envied Him and roused the children of Yashar'el (Israel) against Him, not knowing who He was, and they delivered Him to the king, and crucified Him, and He descended to the angel of Sheol.* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:19). Matthew closes the day with the body laid in a new tomb cut in the rock and a great stone rolled to the door. The Ascension of Isaiah tells where the Beloved was while the body lay there: after they crucified Him, He descended to the angel of Sheol. The same verse says the adversary envied him and stirred up the children of Yashar'el (Israel) against him, not knowing who He was. The charge lies with the adversary who envied and stirred, and a people who did not know who they were handing over are the lost sheep, not enemies.$n$,$n$And after this the adversary envied Him and roused the children of Yashar'el (Israel) against Him, not knowing who He was, and they delivered Him to the king, and crucified Him, and He descended to the angel of Sheol.$n$,true),
(4894,'T','ascension-isaiah',11,21,'ascension-isaiah',11,21,$n$*He is not here: for he is risen, as he said. Come, see the place where Yahusha (Lord) lay.* (Matthew 28:6). *And likewise after the third day rise again and remain days.* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:21). At the empty tomb the angel says that he is not here, for he is risen, as he said. The Ascension of Isaiah has Isaiah told the same in vision, that He will rise after the third day and remain days. The rising was not an afterthought, it was said before by Yahusha (Jesus) himself and seen before by the prophet, and the days he remained with his own after rising are the days the vision speaks of.$n$,$n$And likewise after the third day rise again and remain days.$n$,true),
(4895,'T','ascension-isaiah',11,19,'ascension-isaiah',11,19,$n$*Now when they were going, behold, some of the watch came into the city, and shewed unto the chief priests all the things that were done.* (Matthew 28:11). *And after this the adversary envied Him and roused the children of Yashar'el (Israel) against Him, not knowing who He was, and they delivered Him to the king, and crucified Him, and He descended to the angel of Sheol.* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:19). Matthew tells that some of the watch came into the city and showed the chief priests all that had been done, and the verses that follow tell of money given to the soldiers to carry a false story. The Ascension of Isaiah gives the order of it: the adversary envied him and roused the children of Yashar'el (Israel) against him, not knowing who He was. The line runs from the adversary through those who held the seat of leadership, and the many who were roused did not know, and are deceived sheep. It is a system that lied, and no verse here makes a whole people the enemy.$n$,$n$And after this the adversary envied Him and roused the children of Yashar'el (Israel) against Him, not knowing who He was, and they delivered Him to the king, and crucified Him, and He descended to the angel of Sheol.$n$,true),
(4896,'T','ascension-isaiah',11,22,'ascension-isaiah',11,22,$n$*Go ye therefore, and teach all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit):* (Matthew 28:19). *And the angel who conducted me said: "Understand, Isaiah": and I saw when He sent out the Twelve Apostles and ascended.* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:22). Isaiah sees Him send out the Twelve Apostles and then ascend, and Matthew has the sending in his own words: Go ye therefore, and teach all nations. Twelve are sent because the twelve tribes are the ones being sought, and the nations are where the scattered of those tribes now live. We do not know the sheep by sight, so the word goes out broadly, and the sheep hear his voice.$n$,$n$And the angel who conducted me said: "Understand, Isaiah": and I saw when He sent out the Twelve Apostles and ascended.$n$,true),
(4897,'T','ascension-isaiah',11,32,'ascension-isaiah',11,32,$n$*And Yahusha (Jesus) came and spake unto them, saying, All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth.* (Matthew 28:18). *And I saw how He ascended into the seventh heaven, and all the righteous and all the angels praised Him. And then I saw Him sit down on the right hand of that Great Glory whose glory I told you that I could not behold.* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:32). The Ascension of Isaiah says He sat down on the right hand of that Great Glory whose glory the prophet could not behold. The Great Glory is the Father, the formless one, and the Son who took form sits at his right hand. When Yahusha (Jesus) says in Matthew that all power is given unto him in heaven and in earth, the word given tells the same story: the Son receives the power from the Father who gives it, and takes his seat beside him.$n$,$n$And I saw how He ascended into the seventh heaven, and all the righteous and all the angels praised Him. And then I saw Him sit down on the right hand of that Great Glory whose glory I told you that I could not behold.$n$,true),
(49198,'S','ascension-isaiah',1,13,'ascension-isaiah',1,13,$n$2 Timothy 4:8 — *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahusha (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing.* The "heritage of the Beloved" Isaiah expects to inherit (Ascension of Isaiah 1:13) is this laid-up reward.$n$,$n$And Isaiah said to Hezekiah: `The Beloved hath made of none effect thy design, and the purpose of thy heart will not be accomplished, for with this calling have I been called and I shall inherit the heritage of the Beloved.'$n$,false),
(49199,'S','ascension-isaiah',1,13,'ascension-isaiah',1,7,$n$2 Timothy 4:6 — *For I am now ready to be offered, and the time of my departure is at hand.* Paul names his death "departure" as Isaiah names his — "I shall depart" — embracing it as appointed (Ascension of Isaiah 1:7).$n$,$n$Isaiah said to Hezekiah the king, but not in the presence of Manasseh only did he say unto him: `As Yahuah (Lord) liveth, and the Spirit which speaketh in me liveth, all these commands and these words will be made of none effect by Manasseh thy son, and through the agency of his hands I shall depart mid the torture of my body.$n$,false),
(49208,'S','ascension-isaiah',1,3,'ascension-isaiah',1,3,$n$Ephesians 6:12 — *For we wrestle not against flesh and blood, but against principalities, against powers, against the rulers of the darkness of this world, against spiritual wickedness in high places.* Paul names the same "his angels, and his authorities and his powers" Isaiah saw under the prince of this world in Ascension of Isaiah 1:3.$n$,$n$And of the eternal judgments and torments of Gehenna, and of the prince of this world, and of his angels, and his authorities and his powers.$n$,false),
(49261,'S','ascension-isaiah',4,14,'ascension-isaiah',4,14,$n$2 Thessalonians 2:8 — *And then shall that Wicked be revealed, whom Yahusha (Lord) shall consume with the spirit of his mouth, and shall destroy with the brightness of his coming:* Paul's destruction of the Wicked by the Lord's coming is the same drag of Beliar into Gehenna in Ascension of Isaiah 4:14.$n$,$n$And after three hundred and thirty-two days (Charles inserts "one thousand" here: "after one thousand three hundred and thirty-two days"; the Ethiopic reads three hundred and thirty-two) Yahuah (Lord) will come with His angels and with the armies of the holy ones from the seventh heaven with the glory of the seventh heaven, and He will drag Beliar into Gehenna and also his armies.$n$,false),
(49262,'S','ascension-isaiah',4,14,'ascension-isaiah',4,14,$n$Jude 1:14 — *And Enoch also, the seventh from Adam, prophesied of these, saying, Behold, Yahuah (Lord) cometh with ten thousands of his saints,* Jude's word from Enoch sits beside the Ascension of Isaiah, where Yahuah (the Lord) comes with his angels and with the armies of the holy ones from the seventh heaven. The ten thousands of his saints are the company Enoch saw coming with him — *and all the saints with thee* (Zechariah 14:5) — the coming Enoch foresaw and Isaiah was shown.$n$,$n$And after three hundred and thirty-two days (Charles inserts "one thousand" here: "after one thousand three hundred and thirty-two days"; the Ethiopic reads three hundred and thirty-two) Yahuah (Lord) will come with His angels and with the armies of the holy ones from the seventh heaven with the glory of the seventh heaven, and He will drag Beliar into Gehenna and also his armies.$n$,false),
(49265,'S','ascension-isaiah',4,17,'ascension-isaiah',4,17,$n$1 Thessalonians 4:17 — *Then we which are alive and remain shall be caught up together with them in the clouds, to meet Yahusha (Lord) in the air: and so shall we ever be with Yahusha (Lord).* The catching-up to meet the Lord is the saints turning themselves upward in their garments in Ascension of Isaiah 4:17.$n$,$n$And afterwards they will turn themselves upward in their garments, and their body will be left in the world.$n$,false),
(49281,'S','ascension-isaiah',6,9,'ascension-isaiah',6,9,$n$Amos 3:7 — *Surely Adonai Yahuah (the Lord GOD) does nothing without first revealing his secret unto his servants the prophets.* The door bestowed in an alien world upon a man (6:9) is the secret Yahuah opens only to His servant-prophets.$n$,$n$And they gave glory to Him who had thus bestowed a door in an alien world had bestowed it on a man.$n$,false),
(49299,'S','ascension-isaiah',7,23,'ascension-isaiah',7,23,$n$2 Timothy 4:8 — *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahusha (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing.* The crown laid up for them that love His appearing matches the reward for those who love the Most High and His Beloved in Ascension of Isaiah 7:23.$n$,$n$And I rejoiced with great joy, that those who love the Most High and His Beloved will afterwards ascend thither by the angel of the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit).$n$,false),
(49310,'S','ascension-isaiah',8,14,'ascension-isaiah',8,14,$n$2 Timothy 4:8 — *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahusha (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing.* The numbered garments and crowns laid up for the faithful (8:14, 8:26) are Paul's same laid-up crown of righteousness.$n$,$n$And he said: "Hear, furthermore, therefore, this also from thy fellow servant: when from the body by the will of Elohim (God) thou hast ascended hither, then thou wilt receive the garment which thou seest, and likewise other numbered garments laid up there thou wilt see.$n$,false),
(49334,'S','ascension-isaiah',9,8,'ascension-isaiah',9,8,$n$Hebrews 11:5 — *By faith Enoch was translated that he should not see death; and was not found, because Elohim (God) had translated him: for before his translation he had this testimony, that he pleased Elohim (God).* The very Enoch Isaiah sees 'in their garments of the upper world' (9:8) is the Enoch Scripture says was translated for pleasing Elohim — it ain't new.$n$,$n$And there I saw Enoch and all who were with him, stript of the garments of the flesh, and I saw them in their garments of the upper world, and they were like angels, standing there in great glory.$n$,false),
(49339,'S','ascension-isaiah',9,15,'ascension-isaiah',9,15,$n$*And thus His descent, as you will see, will be hidden even from the heavens, so that it will not be known who He is.* (Ascension of Isaiah 9:15). *For he shall grow up before him as a tender plant, and as a root out of a dry ground: he hath no form nor comeliness; and when we shall see him, there is no beauty that we should desire him.* (Isaiah 53:2). The Ascension of Isaiah says the Son's coming down will be hidden even from the heavens, so that none will know who He is. Isaiah had already spoken of this long before, of one who grows up like a tender plant, with no form or comeliness to draw the eye. The powers of heaven did not recognize him as he passed through, and the people on earth did not see anything in him to desire.$n$,$n$And thus His descent, as you will see, will be hidden even from the heavens, so that it will not be known who He is.$n$,true),
(49341,'S','ascension-isaiah',9,14,'ascension-isaiah',9,14,$n$1 Corinthians 2:8 — *Which none of the princes of this world knew: for had they known it, they would not have crucified Adonai (Lord) of glory.* Paul says exactly what 9:14 foretells: they 'slay Him not knowing who He is' — the Lord of glory crucified by a world blind to His descent.$n$,$n$And the god of that world will stretch forth his hand against the Son, and they will crucify Him on a tree, and will slay Him not knowing who He is.$n$,false),
(49342,'S','ascension-isaiah',9,5,'ascension-isaiah',9,5,$n$John 17:5 — *And now, O Father, glorify thou me with thine own self with the glory which I had with thee before the world was.* The hidden name Isaiah 'canst not hear till thou hast ascended' is the glory the Son had with the Father before the world — the Formed Son asking the Father for what was already His.$n$,$n$And He who permitted thee, this is thy Yahuah Elohim (LORD God), Yahuah (Lord) Messiah (Christ), who will be called 'Jesus' in the world, but His name thou canst not hear till thou hast ascended out of thy body."$n$,false),
(49358,'S','ascension-isaiah',10,11,'ascension-isaiah',10,11,$n$1 Corinthians 2:8 — *Which none of the princes of this world knew: for had they known it, they would not have crucified Adonai (Lord) of glory.* Exactly the Ascension's logic: the Beloved was so transformed (10:11) that the rulers did not know Him — had they known, they would not have crucified Him.$n$,$n$And none of the angels of that world shall know that Thou art with Me of the seven heavens and of their angels.$n$,false),
(49371,'S','ascension-isaiah',11,16,'ascension-isaiah',11,16,$n$1 Corinthians 2:8 — *Which none of the princes of this world knew: for had they known it, they would not have crucified Adonai (Lord) of glory.* The descent that escaped all the princes of this world is why they crucified the Lord of glory unknowing.$n$,$n$And I saw, O Hezekiah and Josab my son, and I declare to the other prophets also who are standing by, that this hath escaped all the heavens and all the princes and all the gods of this world.$n$,false),
(49380,'S','ascension-isaiah',11,26,'ascension-isaiah',11,26,$n$*Both worshipped Him and praised Him and said: "How did our Lord escape us whilst descending, and we perceived not?"* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:26). *Saying with a loud voice, Worthy is the Lamb that was slain to receive power, and riches, and wisdom, and strength, and honour, and glory, and blessing.* (Revelation 5:12). In the Ascension of Isaiah, the powers of the heavens worship the Beloved as he passes through and ask how He went by them unseen, and at each heaven the same praise is given again. John's vision of the throne room has the same voice going up, loud and many: Worthy is the Lamb that was slain. The praise the angels give in Isaiah's vision is the praise of Revelation, given to the one who was slain.$n$,$n$Both worshipped Him and praised Him and said: "How did our Lord escape us whilst descending, and we perceived not?"$n$,true),
(49385,'S','ascension-isaiah',11,40,'ascension-isaiah',11,40,$n$2 Timothy 4:8 — *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahusha (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing.* The crowns of glory laid up in the seventh heaven are Paul's crown of righteousness laid up for them that love His appearing.$n$,$n$Such things ye will read. And watch ye in the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit) in order that ye may receive your garments and thrones and crowns of glory which are laid up in the seventh heaven.$n$,false);
CREATE TEMP TABLE _s463eim (thread_id INT, xid INT, new_note TEXT) ON COMMIT DROP;
INSERT INTO _s463eim VALUES
(45,4317,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 3:13 — *the going forth of the Beloved from the seventh heaven had been made known.* The Beloved whose descent enraged Beliar sends Satan away with the Torah's own word.$n$),
(45,4315,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 4:2 — *Beliar the great ruler, the king of this world, will descend, who hath ruled it since it came into being.* The Ascension of Isaiah names the one who has ruled this world from the beginning, and the devil offers Yahusha (Jesus) what he holds.$n$),
(116,4457,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 4:3 — *Of the Twelve one will be delivered into his hands.* The persecution of the plant and the loss of one of the Twelve were told in advance, and Matthew's list ends on the one who betrayed.$n$),
(45,4316,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 4:9 — *those who shall have been associated together in order to receive the Beloved, he will turn aside after him.* The ruler who asked the Son for worship turns aside the greater number of those gathered to receive the Beloved.$n$),
(420,4885,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 9:14 — *will stretch forth his hand against the Son, and they will crucify Him on a tree.* The deed is traced to the god of that world, and those who did it did not know who He was.$n$),
(11972,49339,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 9:15 — *His descent, as you will see, will be hidden even from the heavens.* The descent hidden from the heavens matches Isaiah's tender plant with no form or comeliness.$n$),
(420,4886,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 9:16 — *when He hath plundered the angel of death, He will ascend on the third day.* The Son who yielded up the ghost at the cross plunders the angel of death and rises on the third day.$n$),
(420,4887,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 9:17 — *many of the righteous will ascend with Him, whose spirits do not receive their garments.* The righteous who sleep wait for the Messiah's ascension, and Matthew shows the first of them rising.$n$),
(420,4889,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 11:19 — *they delivered Him to the king, and crucified Him, and He descended to the angel of Sheol.* While the body lay in the sealed tomb, the Beloved went down to the angel of Sheol.$n$),
(422,4895,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 11:19 — *the adversary envied Him and roused the children of Yashar'el (Israel) against Him, not knowing who He was.* The adversary roused the people not knowing who He was, and Matthew shows the leadership answering the truth with a cover story.$n$),
(420,4888,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 11:20 — *In Jerusalem indeed I saw Him being crucified on a tree.* Isaiah is shown the crucifixion ahead of time, in Jerusalem, on a tree.$n$),
(422,4894,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 11:21 — *after the third day rise again and remain days.* Isaiah is shown the rising after the third day and the days He remained, which the angel at the tomb announces as fulfilled.$n$),
(422,4896,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 11:22 — *I saw when He sent out the Twelve Apostles and ascended.* The sending of the Twelve and the ascension are seen together, as Matthew's last words to the Twelve are spoken.$n$),
(11985,49380,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 11:26 — *How did our Lord escape us whilst descending, and we perceived not?* The heavens worship the Beloved who passed through unseen, as they cry Worthy is the Lamb in Revelation.$n$),
(422,4897,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 11:32 — *I saw Him sit down on the right hand of that Great Glory.* The Son sits at the right hand of the Great Glory, the Father, and Matthew has him say that all power is given unto him.$n$),
(11934,49198,$n$2 Timothy 4:8 — *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahusha (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing.* The "heritage of the Beloved" Isaiah expects to inherit (Ascension of Isaiah 1:13) is this laid-up reward.$n$),
(11949,49261,$n$2 Thessalonians 2:8 — *And then shall that Wicked be revealed, whom Yahusha (Lord) shall consume with the spirit of his mouth, and shall destroy with the brightness of his coming:* Paul's destruction of the Wicked by the Lord's coming is the same drag of Beliar into Gehenna in Ascension of Isaiah 4:14.$n$),
(11950,49265,$n$1 Thessalonians 4:17 — *Then we which are alive and remain shall be caught up together with them in the clouds, to meet Yahusha (Lord) in the air: and so shall we ever be with Yahusha (Lord).* The catching-up to meet the Lord is the saints turning themselves upward in their garments in Ascension of Isaiah 4:17.$n$),
(11958,49281,$n$Amos 3:7 — *Surely Adonai Yahuah (the Lord GOD) does nothing without first revealing his secret unto his servants the prophets.* The door bestowed in an alien world upon a man (6:9) is the secret Yahuah opens only to His servant-prophets.$n$),
(11962,49299,$n$2 Timothy 4:8 — *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahusha (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing.* The crown laid up for them that love His appearing matches the reward for those who love the Most High and His Beloved in Ascension of Isaiah 7:23.$n$),
(11970,49310,$n$2 Timothy 4:8 — *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahusha (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing.* The numbered garments and crowns laid up for the faithful (8:14, 8:26) are Paul's same laid-up crown of righteousness.$n$),
(11972,49341,$n$1 Corinthians 2:8 — *Which none of the princes of this world knew: for had they known it, they would not have crucified Adonai (Lord) of glory.* Paul says exactly what 9:14 foretells: they 'slay Him not knowing who He is' — the Lord of glory crucified by a world blind to His descent.$n$),
(11977,49358,$n$1 Corinthians 2:8 — *Which none of the princes of this world knew: for had they known it, they would not have crucified Adonai (Lord) of glory.* Exactly the Ascension's logic: the Beloved was so transformed (10:11) that the rulers did not know Him — had they known, they would not have crucified Him.$n$),
(11983,49371,$n$1 Corinthians 2:8 — *Which none of the princes of this world knew: for had they known it, they would not have crucified Adonai (Lord) of glory.* The descent that escaped all the princes of this world is why they crucified the Lord of glory unknowing.$n$),
(11987,49385,$n$2 Timothy 4:8 — *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahusha (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing.* The crowns of glory laid up in the seventh heaven are Paul's crown of righteousness laid up for them that love His appearing.$n$),
(12141,50079,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 9:8 — *Enoch and all who were with him, stript of the garments of the flesh ... in their garments of the upper world ... standing there in great glory* — the company paradise gathers, the same place Paul *was caught up into... and heard unspeakable words* (2 Corinthians 12:4).$n$),
(11934,49199,$n$2 Timothy 4:6 — *For I am now ready to be offered, and the time of my departure is at hand.* Paul names his death "departure" as Isaiah names his — "I shall depart" — embracing it as appointed (Ascension of Isaiah 1:7).$n$),
(11931,49208,$n$Ephesians 6:12 — *For we wrestle not against flesh and blood, but against principalities, against powers, against the rulers of the darkness of this world, against spiritual wickedness in high places.* Paul names the same "his angels, and his authorities and his powers" Isaiah saw under the prince of this world in Ascension of Isaiah 1:3.$n$),
(11949,49262,$n$Jude 1:14 — *And Enoch also, the seventh from Adam, prophesied of these, saying, Behold, Yahuah (Lord) cometh with ten thousands of his saints,* Jude's word from Enoch sits beside the Ascension of Isaiah, where Yahuah (the Lord) comes with his angels and with the armies of the holy ones from the seventh heaven. The ten thousands of his saints are the company Enoch saw coming with him — *and all the saints with thee* (Zechariah 14:5) — the coming Enoch foresaw and Isaiah was shown.$n$),
(11974,49334,$n$Hebrews 11:5 — *By faith Enoch was translated that he should not see death; and was not found, because Elohim (God) had translated him: for before his translation he had this testimony, that he pleased Elohim (God).* The very Enoch Isaiah sees 'in their garments of the upper world' (9:8) is the Enoch Scripture says was translated for pleasing Elohim — it ain't new.$n$),
(11971,49342,$n$John 17:5 — *And now, O Father, glorify thou me with thine own self with the glory which I had with thee before the world was.* The hidden name Isaiah 'canst not hear till thou hast ascended' is the glory the Son had with the Father before the world — the Formed Son asking the Father for what was already His.$n$),
(33,4277,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 10:8 — *Go forth and descend through all the heavens, and thou wilt descend to the firmament and that world.* The Father sends the Beloved down through the heavens, and Matthew 1:23 names where the descent ends: *Elohim (God) with us.*$n$),
(41,4300,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 9:12 — *Crowns and thrones of glory they do not receive, till the Beloved will descend.* Heaven announces beforehand the Beloved's coming down in human form, and at the water the voice from heaven says, *This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased* (Matthew 3:17).$n$),
(41,4301,$n$Ascension of Isaiah 11:32 — *And then I saw Him sit down on the right hand of that Great Glory.* The Son whom the voice from heaven names at the water (Matthew 3:17) is seen here with his journey down and back up finished, seated beside the Great Glory.$n$);
CREATE TEMP TABLE _s463eis (thread_id INT, old_summary TEXT, new_summary TEXT) ON COMMIT DROP;
INSERT INTO _s463eis VALUES
(11959,$n$The guiding angel keeps the order of heaven exactly as Yoshi reads it: *And His Father also who is greater thou wilt see; for for this purpose have I been sent from the seventh heaven in order to explain all these things unto thee.* (Ascension of Isaiah 7:8). The one who descends is **sent** and has a **Father who is greater** — the Formed Son ordered under the Most High, not a co-equal person and not the Father Himself. It ain't new: the Word was *with* Elohim and made flesh by the Father's purpose — *He that descended is the same also that ascended up far above all heavens, that he might fill all things.* (Ephesians 4:10); *Wherefore Elohim (God) also hath highly exalted him, and given him a name which is above every name:* (Philippians 2:9); and the Son Himself names the glory He had *with* the Father before the descent — *And now, O Father, glorify thou me with thine own self with the glory which I had with thee before the world was.* (John 17:5).$n$,$n$The guiding angel keeps the order of heaven plain: *And His Father also who is greater thou wilt see; for for this purpose have I been sent from the seventh heaven in order to explain all these things unto thee.* (Ascension of Isaiah 7:8). The one who descends is **sent** and has a **Father who is greater** — the Formed Son ordered under the Most High, not a co-equal person and not the Father Himself. It ain't new: the Word was *with* Elohim (God) and made flesh by the Father's purpose — *He that descended is the same also that ascended up far above all heavens, that he might fill all things.* (Ephesians 4:10); *Wherefore Elohim (God) also hath highly exalted him, and given him a name which is above every name:* (Philippians 2:9); and the Son Himself names the glory He had *with* the Father before the descent — *And now, O Father, glorify thou me with thine own self with the glory which I had with thee before the world was.* (John 17:5).$n$),
(11975,$n$The climax guards the order of worship. First the Beloved is worshipped at the Father's command: *And thereupon the angel who conducted me said to me: "Worship this One," and I worshipped and praised.* (Ascension of Isaiah 9:31). Then the angel of the Spirit on the left (9:36). But above both stands the Great Glory whom none can behold (9:37) — and the Beloved Himself worships Him: *And I saw how my Lord and the angel of the Spirit worshipped, and they both together praised Elohim (God).* (Ascension of Isaiah 9:40). This is Yoshi's Formed-Son order exactly: the Son is worshipped at the Father's word, yet the Son worships the Father. It ain't new. The Father commands the heavens to bow to the firstbegotten, *And again, when he bringeth in the firstbegotten into the world, he saith, And let all the angels of Elohim (God) worship him.* (Hebrews 1:6); every knee bows at His name *to the glory of Elohim (God) the Father* — *And that every tongue should confess that Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ) is Lord, to the glory of Elohim (God) the Father.* (Philippians 2:11). John's throne-room keeps the same two-fold order, blessing to Him on the throne AND to the Lamb, *And every creature which is in heaven, and on the earth, and under the earth, and such as are in the sea, and all that are in them, heard I saying, Blessing, and honour, and glory, and power, be unto him that sitteth upon the throne, and unto the Lamb for ever and ever.* (Revelation 5:13). Not flattened to co-equality, not denied His exaltation — the Beloved exalted by, and bowing to, the One.$n$,$n$The climax guards the order of worship. First the Beloved is worshipped at the Father's command: *And thereupon the angel who conducted me said to me: "Worship this One," and I worshipped and praised.* (Ascension of Isaiah 9:31). Then the angel of the Spirit on the left (Ascension of Isaiah 9:36). But above both stands the Great Glory whom none can behold (Ascension of Isaiah 9:37) — and the Beloved Himself worships Him: *And I saw how my Lord and the angel of the Spirit worshipped, and they both together praised Elohim (God).* (Ascension of Isaiah 9:40). This is the order exactly: the Son is worshipped at the Father's word, yet the Son worships the Father. It ain't new. The Father commands the heavens to bow to the firstbegotten, *And again, when he bringeth in the firstbegotten into the world, he saith, And let all the angels of Elohim (God) worship him.* (Hebrews 1:6); every knee bows at His name *to the glory of Elohim (God) the Father* — *And that every tongue should confess that Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ) is Lord, to the glory of Elohim (God) the Father.* (Philippians 2:11). John's throne-room keeps the same twofold order, blessing to Him on the throne AND to the Lamb, *And every creature which is in heaven, and on the earth, and under the earth, and such as are in the sea, and all that are in them, heard I saying, Blessing, and honour, and glory, and power, be unto him that sitteth upon the throne, and unto the Lamb for ever and ever.* (Revelation 5:13). Not flattened to co-equality, not denied His exaltation — the Beloved exalted by, and bowing to, the One.$n$),
(11934,$n$Isaiah does not flee his end; he names it as a calling: *through the agency of his hands I shall depart mid the torture of my body*, and *with this calling have I been called and I shall inherit the heritage of the Beloved*. The martyr's death is the martyr's portion. It ain't new. Paul faces his own offering in the same key: *For I am now ready to be offered, and the time of my departure is at hand* (2 Timothy 4:6), *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahuah (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day* (2 Timothy 4:8). And those who suffered the saw obtained the better portion: *and others were tortured, not accepting deliverance; that they might obtain a better resurrection* (Hebrews 11:35) — the heritage of the Beloved Isaiah was content to inherit.$n$,$n$Isaiah does not flee his end; he names it as a calling: *through the agency of his hands I shall depart mid the torture of my body*, and *with this calling have I been called and I shall inherit the heritage of the Beloved*. The martyr's death is the martyr's portion. It ain't new. Paul faces his own offering in the same key: *For I am now ready to be offered, and the time of my departure is at hand* (2 Timothy 4:6), *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahusha (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day* (2 Timothy 4:8). And those who suffered the saw obtained the better portion: *and others were tortured, not accepting deliverance; that they might obtain a better resurrection* (Hebrews 11:35) — the heritage of the Beloved Isaiah was content to inherit.$n$),
(11949,$n$*Yahuah (Lord) will come with His angels and with the armies of the holy ones from the seventh heaven with the glory of the seventh heaven, and He will drag Beliar into Gehenna and also his armies* (Ascension of Isaiah 4:14). At his coming the lawless one is destroyed: *the armies which were in heaven followed him upon white horses* (Revelation 19:14), and the beast out of the sea and the false prophet *were cast alive into a lake of fire burning with brimstone* (Revelation 19:20). Paul: *that Wicked... whom Yahuah (Lord) shall consume with the spirit of his mouth, and shall destroy with the brightness of his coming* (2 Thessalonians 2:8). Enoch the seventh from Adam said the same — *Behold, Yahuah (Lord) cometh with ten thousands of his saints* (Jude 14). The saints who come with him are the seed of promise, gathered and coming with him into the land — *Yahuah Elohai (the LORD my God) shall come, and all the saints with thee* (Zechariah 14:5) — not souls come down from heaven; no other scripture has anyone coming down from the sky with him. It ain't new.$n$,$n$*Yahuah (Lord) will come with His angels and with the armies of the holy ones from the seventh heaven with the glory of the seventh heaven, and He will drag Beliar into Gehenna and also his armies* (Ascension of Isaiah 4:14). At his coming the lawless one is destroyed: *the armies which were in heaven followed him upon white horses* (Revelation 19:14), and the beast out of the sea and the false prophet *were cast alive into a lake of fire burning with brimstone* (Revelation 19:20). Paul: *that Wicked be revealed, whom Yahusha (Lord) shall consume with the spirit of his mouth, and shall destroy with the brightness of his coming* (2 Thessalonians 2:8). Enoch the seventh from Adam said the same — *Behold, Yahuah (Lord) cometh with ten thousands of his saints* (Jude 14). The saints who come with him are the seed of promise, gathered and coming with him into the land — *Yahuah Elohai (the LORD my God) shall come, and all the saints with thee* (Zechariah 14:5) — not souls come down from heaven; no other scripture has anyone coming down from the sky with him. It ain't new.$n$),
(11958,$n$Forty prophets and sons of the prophets gather, *that he might place his hands upon them, and that they might prophesy* (Ascension of Isaiah 6:5). It ain't new — this is the company Samuel knew, where *the Spirit of Yahuah (LORD) will come upon thee, and thou shalt prophesy with them, and shalt be turned into another man* (1 Samuel 10:6). And the door opened in Isaiah's hearing is the same Spirit foretold by Joel and poured out at Pentecost: *I will pour out of my Spirit upon all flesh: and your sons and your daughters shall prophesy, and your young men shall see visions* (Acts 2:17). The Most High *revealeth his secret unto his servants the prophets* (Amos 3:7) — and so He bestowed *a door in an alien world* upon a man (Ascension of Isaiah 6:9).$n$,$n$Forty prophets and sons of the prophets gather, *that he might place his hands upon them, and that they might prophesy* (Ascension of Isaiah 6:5). It ain't new — this is the company Samuel knew, where *the Spirit of Yahuah (LORD) will come upon thee, and thou shalt prophesy with them, and shalt be turned into another man* (1 Samuel 10:6). And the door opened in Isaiah's hearing is the same Spirit foretold by Joel and poured out at Pentecost: *I will pour out of my Spirit upon all flesh: and your sons and your daughters shall prophesy, and your young men shall see visions* (Acts 2:17). The Most High *does nothing without first revealing his secret unto his servants the prophets* (Amos 3:7) — and so He bestowed *a door in an alien world* upon a man (Ascension of Isaiah 6:9).$n$),
(11962,$n$The angel forbids worship of any throne or angel of the six heavens, then reveals what is kept for the righteous: *For above all the heavens and their angels has thy throne been placed, and thy garments and thy crown which thou shalt see.* (Ascension of Isaiah 7:22); and the ascent belongs to those who love the Most High and His Beloved: *And I rejoiced with great joy, that those who love the Most High and His Beloved will afterwards ascend thither by the angel of the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit).* (Ascension of Isaiah 7:23). It ain't new — the throne, the white robe and the crown are already laid up: *And round about the throne were four and twenty seats: and upon the seats I saw four and twenty elders sitting, clothed in white raiment; and they had on their heads crowns of gold.* (Revelation 4:4); *He that overcometh, the same shall be clothed in white raiment; and I will not blot out his name out of the book of life, but I will confess his name before my Father, and before his angels.* (Revelation 3:5); *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahuah (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing.* (2 Timothy 4:8).$n$,$n$The angel forbids worship of any throne or angel of the six heavens, then reveals what is kept for the righteous: *For above all the heavens and their angels has thy throne been placed, and thy garments and thy crown which thou shalt see.* (Ascension of Isaiah 7:22); and the ascent belongs to those who love the Most High and His Beloved: *And I rejoiced with great joy, that those who love the Most High and His Beloved will afterwards ascend thither by the angel of the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit).* (Ascension of Isaiah 7:23). It ain't new — the throne, the white robe and the crown are already laid up: *And round about the throne were four and twenty seats: and upon the seats I saw four and twenty elders sitting, clothed in white raiment; and they had on their heads crowns of gold.* (Revelation 4:4); *He that overcometh, the same shall be clothed in white raiment; and I will not blot out his name out of the book of life, but I will confess his name before my Father, and before his angels.* (Revelation 3:5); *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahusha (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing.* (2 Timothy 4:8).$n$),
(11970,$n$Isaiah is promised the reward kept above for the faithful: *then thou wilt receive the garment which thou seest, and likewise other numbered garments laid up there thou wilt see* (Ascension of Isaiah 8:14), *the garments, and the thrones, and the crowns which are laid up for the righteous, for those who trust in that Yahuah (Lord) who will descend in your form* (Ascension of Isaiah 8:26). It ain't new — the overcomers are clothed in white and crowned: *And to her was granted that she should be arrayed in fine linen, clean and white: for the fine linen is the righteousness of saints* (Revelation 19:8), and the laid-up reward is the believer's hope: *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahuah (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing* (2 Timothy 4:8).$n$,$n$Isaiah is promised the reward kept above for the faithful: *then thou wilt receive the garment which thou seest, and likewise other numbered garments laid up there thou wilt see* (Ascension of Isaiah 8:14), *the garments, and the thrones, and the crowns which are laid up for the righteous, for those who trust in that Yahuah (Lord) who will descend in your form* (Ascension of Isaiah 8:26). It ain't new — the overcomers are clothed in white and crowned: *And to her was granted that she should be arrayed in fine linen, clean and white: for the fine linen is the righteousness of saints* (Revelation 19:8), and the laid-up reward is the believer's hope: *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahusha (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing* (2 Timothy 4:8).$n$),
(11972,$n$The angel foretells the Beloved's descent in disguise: *And the god of that world will stretch forth his hand against the Son, and they will crucify Him on a tree, and will slay Him not knowing who He is.* (Ascension of Isaiah 9:14), *And thus His descent, as you will see, will be hidden even from the heavens, so that it will not be known who He is.* (Ascension of Isaiah 9:15). It ain't new — Paul says the very same: the rulers were blind to the Lord of glory, *Which none of the princes of this world knew: for had they known it, they would not have crucified Yahuah (Lord) of glory.* (1 Corinthians 2:8). The Formed Son emptied His likeness through every heaven so the powers would not know Him — *But made himself of no reputation, and took upon him the form of a servant, and was made in the likeness of men:* (Philippians 2:7) — and so He came with *no form nor comeliness* (Isaiah 53:2). This is descent, not demotion: the One who came down is the One who fills all heavens, *(Now that he ascended, what is it but that he also descended first into the lower parts of the earth? He that descended is the same also that ascended up far above all heavens, that he might fill all things.)* (Ephesians 4:9-10).$n$,$n$The angel foretells the Beloved's descent in disguise: *And the god of that world will stretch forth his hand against the Son, and they will crucify Him on a tree, and will slay Him not knowing who He is.* (Ascension of Isaiah 9:14), *And thus His descent, as you will see, will be hidden even from the heavens, so that it will not be known who He is.* (Ascension of Isaiah 9:15). It ain't new — Paul says the very same: the rulers were blind to the Lord of glory, *Which none of the princes of this world knew: for had they known it, they would not have crucified Adonai (Lord) of glory.* (1 Corinthians 2:8). The Formed Son emptied His likeness through every heaven so the powers would not know Him — *But made himself of no reputation, and took upon him the form of a servant, and was made in the likeness of men:* (Philippians 2:7) — and so He came with *no form nor comeliness* (Isaiah 53:2). This is descent, not demotion: the One who came down is the One who fills all heavens, *(Now that he ascended, what is it but that he also descended first into the lower parts of the earth? He that descended is the same also that ascended up far above all heavens, that he might fill all things.)* (Ephesians 4:9-10).$n$),
(11977,$n$The Father orders the Beloved to veil His glory: *And thou wilt become like unto the likeness of all who are in the five heavens.* (Ascension of Isaiah 10:9), *And thou wilt be careful to become like the form of the angels of the firmament and the angels also who are in Sheol.* (Ascension of Isaiah 10:10), *And none of the angels of that world shall know that Thou art with Me of the seven heavens and of their angels.* (Ascension of Isaiah 10:11). It ain't new — this is the hidden glory Paul names: *But we speak the wisdom of Elohim (God) in a mystery, even the hidden wisdom, which Elohim (God) ordained before the world unto our glory:* (1 Corinthians 2:7) — *Which none of the princes of this world knew: for had they known it, they would not have crucified Yahuah (Lord) of glory.* (1 Corinthians 2:8). The veiling is the self-emptying: *But made himself of no reputation, and took upon him the form of a servant, and was made in the likeness of men:* (Philippians 2:7). Isaiah had already foretold the unrecognized form: *For he shall grow up before him as a tender plant, and as a root out of a dry ground: he hath no form nor comeliness; and when we shall see him, there is no beauty that we should desire him.* (Isaiah 53:2). And the Word so veiled was yet the Word made flesh, His glory seen only by faith: *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* (John 1:14).$n$,$n$The Father orders the Beloved to veil His glory: *And thou wilt become like unto the likeness of all who are in the five heavens.* (Ascension of Isaiah 10:9), *And thou wilt be careful to become like the form of the angels of the firmament and the angels also who are in Sheol.* (Ascension of Isaiah 10:10), *And none of the angels of that world shall know that Thou art with Me of the seven heavens and of their angels.* (Ascension of Isaiah 10:11). It ain't new — this is the hidden glory Paul names: *But we speak the wisdom of Elohim (God) in a mystery, even the hidden wisdom, which Elohim (God) ordained before the world unto our glory:* (1 Corinthians 2:7) — *Which none of the princes of this world knew: for had they known it, they would not have crucified Adonai (Lord) of glory.* (1 Corinthians 2:8). The veiling is the self-emptying: *But made himself of no reputation, and took upon him the form of a servant, and was made in the likeness of men:* (Philippians 2:7). Isaiah had already foretold the unrecognized form: *For he shall grow up before him as a tender plant, and as a root out of a dry ground: he hath no form nor comeliness; and when we shall see him, there is no beauty that we should desire him.* (Isaiah 53:2). And the Word so veiled was yet the Word made flesh, His glory seen only by faith: *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* (John 1:14).$n$),
(11983,$n$The Beloved came down veiled, unrecognised even at His birth: *And many said: "She has not borne a child, nor has a midwife gone up to her, nor have we heard the cries of labour pains." And they were all blinded respecting Him and they all knew regarding Him, though they knew not whence He was.* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:14). The descent itself escaped the heavens and the rulers: *And I saw, O Hezekiah and Josab my son, and I declare to the other prophets also who are standing by, that this hath escaped all the heavens and all the princes and all the gods of this world.* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:16). And in Nazareth He concealed His glory: *And I saw: In Nazareth He sucked the breast as a babe and as is customary in order that He might not be recognized.* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:17). Paul declares the very same hiddenness as the reason for the cross: *Which none of the princes of this world knew: for had they known it, they would not have crucified Yahuah (Lord) of glory.* (1 Corinthians 2:8). He made Himself of no reputation and took the form of a servant: *But made himself of no reputation, and took upon him the form of a servant, and was made in the likeness of men:* (Philippians 2:7) — the Formed Son ordered under the Father, emptied that the rulers should not perceive Him. It ain't new: of old He had no comeliness that we should desire Him.$n$,$n$The Beloved came down veiled, unrecognised even at His birth: *And many said: "She has not borne a child, nor has a midwife gone up to her, nor have we heard the cries of labour pains." And they were all blinded respecting Him and they all knew regarding Him, though they knew not whence He was.* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:14). The descent itself escaped the heavens and the rulers: *And I saw, O Hezekiah and Josab my son, and I declare to the other prophets also who are standing by, that this hath escaped all the heavens and all the princes and all the gods of this world.* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:16). And in Nazareth He concealed His glory: *And I saw: In Nazareth He sucked the breast as a babe and as is customary in order that He might not be recognized.* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:17). Paul declares the very same hiddenness as the reason for the cross: *Which none of the princes of this world knew: for had they known it, they would not have crucified Adonai (Lord) of glory.* (1 Corinthians 2:8). He made Himself of no reputation and took the form of a servant: *But made himself of no reputation, and took upon him the form of a servant, and was made in the likeness of men:* (Philippians 2:7) — the Formed Son ordered under the Father, emptied that the rulers should not perceive Him. It ain't new: of old He had no comeliness that we should desire Him.$n$),
(11987,$n$Isaiah is sent back to the flesh with a charge for the readers of the vision: *And thou wilt return into thy garment of the flesh until thy days are completed. Then thou wilt come hither.* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:35), and: *Such things ye will read. And watch ye in the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit) in order that ye may receive your garments and thrones and crowns of glory which are laid up in the seventh heaven.* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:40). The crown laid up is the same Paul awaited: *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahuah (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing.* (2 Timothy 4:8). The white robe is promised to the overcomer: *He that overcometh, the same shall be clothed in white raiment; and I will not blot out his name out of the book of life, but I will confess his name before my Father, and before his angels.* (Revelation 3:5), and the thrones are the elders' seats about the throne: *And round about the throne were four and twenty seats: and upon the seats I saw four and twenty elders sitting, clothed in white raiment; and they had on their heads crowns of gold.* (Revelation 4:4). It ain't new — the reward of the righteous is laid up in heaven and held for the faithful remnant.$n$,$n$Isaiah is sent back to the flesh with a charge for the readers of the vision: *And thou wilt return into thy garment of the flesh until thy days are completed. Then thou wilt come hither.* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:35), and: *Such things ye will read. And watch ye in the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit) in order that ye may receive your garments and thrones and crowns of glory which are laid up in the seventh heaven.* (Ascension of Isaiah 11:40). The crown laid up is the same Paul awaited: *Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which Yahusha (Lord), the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing.* (2 Timothy 4:8). The white robe is promised to the overcomer: *He that overcometh, the same shall be clothed in white raiment; and I will not blot out his name out of the book of life, but I will confess his name before my Father, and before his angels.* (Revelation 3:5), and the thrones are the elders' seats about the throne: *And round about the throne were four and twenty seats: and upon the seats I saw four and twenty elders sitting, clothed in white raiment; and they had on their heads crowns of gold.* (Revelation 4:4). It ain't new — the reward of the righteous is laid up in heaven and held for the faithful remnant.$n$);
CREATE TEMP VIEW _s463eiv AS
  SELECT v.id, e.slug es, b.slug bs, c.chapter_number ch, v.verse_number vn, v.text FROM verses v
    JOIN chapters c ON c.id=v.chapter_id JOIN books b ON b.id=c.book_id JOIN editions e ON e.id=b.edition_id;

DO $fix$
DECLARE r RECORD; cur RECORD; pass INT; nid INT; dup INT;
        n_moved INT := 0; n_requoted INT := 0; n_same INT := 0; n_absent INT := 0; n_skipped INT := 0; n_mem INT := 0; n_sum INT := 0; n_sum_skip INT := 0;
BEGIN
  FOR pass IN 1..3 LOOP
  FOR r IN SELECT * FROM _s463ei ORDER BY xid LOOP
    IF r.side = 'T' THEN
      SELECT x.id, x.note, t.ch, t.vn, t.es, t.bs, x.source_verse_id AS other_id INTO cur
        FROM cross_references x JOIN _s463eiv t ON t.id = x.target_verse_id WHERE x.id = r.xid;
    ELSE
      SELECT x.id, x.note, s.ch, s.vn, s.es, s.bs, x.target_verse_id AS other_id INTO cur
        FROM cross_references x JOIN _s463eiv s ON s.id = x.source_verse_id WHERE x.id = r.xid;
    END IF;
    IF cur.id IS NULL THEN
      IF pass = 3 THEN n_absent := n_absent + 1; RAISE NOTICE 'S463e card % absent', r.xid; END IF; CONTINUE;
    END IF;
    IF cur.es <> 'ascension-isaiah' OR cur.bs <> r.ob THEN
      IF pass = 3 THEN n_skipped := n_skipped + 1; RAISE NOTICE 'S463e card % extra end is %/% not ascension-isaiah/% — skipped', r.xid, cur.es, cur.bs, r.ob; END IF; CONTINUE;
    END IF;
    IF cur.bs = r.nb AND cur.ch = r.nc AND cur.vn = r.nv AND cur.note = r.new_note THEN
      IF pass = 1 THEN n_same := n_same + 1; END IF; CONTINUE;
    END IF;
    IF NOT (cur.ch = r.oc AND cur.vn = r.ov) AND NOT (cur.bs = r.nb AND cur.ch = r.nc AND cur.vn = r.nv) THEN
      IF pass = 3 THEN n_skipped := n_skipped + 1;
      RAISE NOTICE 'S463e card % is at % %:%, expected %:% — edited since the read-back, skipped', r.xid, cur.bs, cur.ch, cur.vn, r.oc, r.ov; END IF; CONTINUE;
    END IF;
    SELECT id INTO nid FROM _s463eiv WHERE es = 'ascension-isaiah' AND bs = r.nb AND ch = r.nc AND vn = r.nv;
    IF nid IS NULL THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'S463e: live % %:% missing', r.nb, r.nc, r.nv; END IF;
    IF (SELECT text FROM _s463eiv WHERE id = nid) <> r.live_text THEN
      RAISE EXCEPTION 'S463e: live % %:% text differs from the read-back the fix was written against — re-run the dump and rebuild', r.nb, r.nc, r.nv;
    END IF;
    IF r.quotes_live AND position(r.live_text IN r.new_note) = 0 THEN
      RAISE EXCEPTION 'S463e: new note for card % does not quote the live % %:% verbatim', r.xid, r.nb, r.nc, r.nv;
    END IF;
    IF nid = cur.other_id THEN
      IF pass = 3 THEN n_skipped := n_skipped + 1; RAISE NOTICE 'S463e SKIPPED card % (-> % %:%): that is the card''s other verse', r.xid, r.nb, r.nc, r.nv; END IF;
      CONTINUE;
    END IF;
    IF r.side = 'T' THEN
      SELECT count(*) INTO dup FROM cross_references x WHERE x.source_verse_id = cur.other_id AND x.target_verse_id = nid AND x.id <> r.xid;
    ELSE
      SELECT count(*) INTO dup FROM cross_references x WHERE x.target_verse_id = cur.other_id AND x.source_verse_id = nid AND x.id <> r.xid;
    END IF;
    IF dup > 0 THEN
      IF pass = 3 THEN n_skipped := n_skipped + 1; RAISE NOTICE 'S463e SKIPPED card % (-> % %:%): a card already sits on that pair', r.xid, r.nb, r.nc, r.nv; END IF;
      CONTINUE;
    END IF;
    IF r.side = 'T' THEN UPDATE cross_references SET target_verse_id = nid, note = r.new_note WHERE id = r.xid;
    ELSE UPDATE cross_references SET source_verse_id = nid, note = r.new_note WHERE id = r.xid; END IF;
    IF r.oc = r.nc AND r.ov = r.nv AND r.ob = r.nb THEN n_requoted := n_requoted + 1;
    ELSE n_moved := n_moved + 1; RAISE NOTICE 'S463e moved card %: % %:% -> %:% (%)', r.xid, r.nb, r.oc, r.ov, r.nc, r.nv, CASE WHEN r.side='T' THEN 'target' ELSE 'source' END; END IF;
  END LOOP;
  END LOOP;

  FOR r IN SELECT m.* FROM _s463eim m LOOP
    UPDATE cross_reference_thread_members SET member_note = r.new_note
     WHERE thread_id = r.thread_id AND cross_reference_id = r.xid AND member_note IS DISTINCT FROM r.new_note;
    IF FOUND THEN n_mem := n_mem + 1; END IF;
  END LOOP;

  FOR r IN SELECT s.* FROM _s463eis s LOOP
    UPDATE cross_reference_threads SET summary_md = r.new_summary WHERE id = r.thread_id AND summary_md = r.old_summary;
    IF FOUND THEN n_sum := n_sum + 1;
    ELSIF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cross_reference_threads WHERE id = r.thread_id AND summary_md = r.new_summary) THEN
      n_sum_skip := n_sum_skip + 1; RAISE NOTICE 'S463e SKIPPED thread % summary: live text is neither the old nor the new', r.thread_id;
    END IF;
  END LOOP;

  RAISE NOTICE 'S463e (ascension-isaiah) summary: notes rewritten in place %, moved %, already landed %, skipped %, absent %; member notes updated %; summaries updated % (skipped %)',
    n_requoted, n_moved, n_same, n_skipped, n_absent, n_mem, n_sum, n_sum_skip;
  IF n_skipped + n_absent + n_sum_skip > 0 THEN RAISE NOTICE 'S463e: read the SKIPPED/absent lines above — those rows still carry the old text'; END IF;
END $fix$;
COMMIT;
\echo 'session463e (ascension-isaiah) — done.'
